{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_fwp_142",
      "name": "menu-virtual-window",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Render only the rows in view",
      "description": "The food-court menu lists up to 3,000 rows: 40 px stall headers and 96 px dishes. Rendering all of them built 45,000 DOM nodes and made scrolling stutter on budget phones; keying rows by index also showed the wrong photos after the vegetarian filter. Complete `visibleWindow(rows, viewport, options)`, the calculation behind the virtualized list. The editor holds `menu/virtualWindow.js` with its key blocks missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Rules: compute each row's top from the heights; the first visible row is the first whose bottom is below `scrollTop` (find it with a binary search, the list is long); rows that start at or below `scrollTop + height` are not visible; add `overscan` rows (default 3) on each side without leaving the list; return `start`, `end` (exclusive), `offsetTop` (top of row `start`), `totalHeight` and the `keys` of rows `start..end-1`, taken from each row's `id`. Run calls it for several scroll positions, list shapes and a filtered list.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "outcomes": [
        "render-efficiency"
      ],
      "points": 40,
      "hints": [
        "Draw the list as stacked boxes with their top positions: which box contains the scroll position, which box starts at the bottom edge, and what happens near position 0 or at the end of the list?",
        "Look at an array of tops with one extra entry (the total height), a `while (lo < hi)` binary search on `tops[mid + 1] <= scrollTop`, `Math.max` / `Math.min` around the overscan, and `row.id` for keys.",
        "Finding which log lines of variable height are on screen in a log viewer looks like: `const tops = [0]; lines.forEach((l, i) => tops.push(tops[i] + l.h));` then a binary search for the first line with `tops[i + 1] > scrollY`, a walk while `tops[j] < scrollY + viewH`, and keys from `line.seq`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "javascript",
        "filePath": "menu/virtualWindow.js",
        "executionMode": "browser",
        "timeLimitMs": 2000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
